# desc: [experimental - needs docker build for patch 23, not benched] DFlash2 draft instead of the MTP head; engine guards opened in-image (vllm#56088); fallback: ./flash serve default
#
# History: the 2026-10-27 GB10 boot showed method=dflash resolving DFlash2DraftModel and the
# YaRN/max_model_len plumbing working, then dying at "Qwen4Exp speculative decoding supports
# only its native MTP checkpoint and linear n-gram proposers" (config.py allowlist = blocker 4 of
# https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm/issues/56088). Patch 23 (src/patch_dflash_qwen4exp.py)
# now opens the allowlist, mounts the EAGLE-3-style target aux-hidden-state capture (incoai's
# completed-layer HC-mean recipe from the draft repo's qwen38-dflash2-capture.patch) and ports
# the QSA ring widening (vllm#54912) for draft depth 7. Rebuild the image after pulling:
#   docker build -t qwen38-flash-dgx:v0.32 .
# PixelML's recipe was measured on 2x GB10 TP2/eager/8k with a DIFFERENT drafter (DeepSpec
# layout); this path is unbenched - the serve log should end with "Using dflash speculative
# decoding" and normal accepted-length behaviour, and ./flash test is the pass gate.
MODE=hybrid
YARN=1
CTX=500000
MTP=0
DRAFT_MODEL=incoai/Qwen3.8-Flash-Next-DFlash2
DRAFT_TOKENS=7
# DFlash2 needs the target's FULL vocabulary (the speculators docs reject pruned draft
# vocabularies), so the MTP-head draft-vocab prune (which defaults to on) is disabled here.
# It only ever applied to the MTP head anyway; set explicitly so the serve line reads truthfully.
DRAFT_VOCAB=0
